    "slug": "microsoft-fabric-certification-roadmap-2026",
    "title": "Build a Microsoft Fabric Study Roadmap from Demonstrated Skills",
    "excerpt": "Choose a learning path by the tasks you can perform, then check the current official certification requirements.",
    "content": "<aside>Worked example with fictional data. AI-assisted editorial revision; no client performance results are claimed.</aside><h2 id=\"section-1\">Begin with a task inventory</h2><p>List the work you want to do: prepare a reliable reporting table, build and secure a semantic model, or operate an ingestion pipeline. Mark each task as demonstrated, assisted or not yet attempted. Owning a list of courses is not the same as being able to complete the task. Use an example you can rebuild rather than collecting screenshots of completed modules.</p><h2 id=\"section-2\">Check the official role descriptions</h2><p>Microsoft publishes separate role and assessment information for Fabric Analytics Engineer and Fabric Data Engineer certifications. Open the current official pages and their linked study guides before planning an exam. Record the date of the skills outline you use. Do not assume that a blog's old comparison matrix, an unofficial exam name or a past promotion reflects the current exam or voucher terms.</p><h2 id=\"section-3\">Plan one evidence-producing exercise</h2><p>For an analytics-oriented path, build a small report with an agreed revenue definition, a model sketch and access tests. For an engineering-oriented path, prepare a replayable import with a control total, rejected-row handling and a failed-run recovery note. Use fictional data. Each exercise should leave artifacts that explain what happened, not just a completion badge.</p><h2 id=\"section-4\">Schedule review instead of promising a deadline</h2><p>Allocate study sessions based on the gaps in the inventory and the time actually available. A person already comfortable with SQL may need a different plan from a report designer learning pipeline operations. Rebuild the exercise without following the instructions, then explain one failure and its correction. Use official practice resources where available, but do not treat memorized questions or a fixed number of study days as a guarantee of passing.</p><h2 id=\"section-5\">Decide when to book</h2><p>Return to the current study guide and map each assessed area to evidence from your work or a remaining gap. Check the official exam language, availability, booking policies and any promotion directly with Microsoft before spending money. The roadmap is a method for making the preparation decision; it does not claim free vouchers, mandatory prerequisite certifications or a guaranteed career outcome.</p><h2 id=\"references\">Primary references</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/certifications/fabric-analytics-engineer-associate/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fabric Analytics Engineer certification</a></li><li><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/certifications/fabric-data-engineer-associate/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fabric Data Engineer certification</a></li></ul>",
