    "slug": "dp-600-study-guide-2026",
    "title": "DP-600 Study Plan: Connect the Official Outline to Practical Evidence",
    "excerpt": "Prepare for Fabric analytics tasks through model, data-quality and access exercises rather than an exam-dump checklist.",
    "content": "<aside>Worked example with fictional data. AI-assisted editorial revision; no client performance results are claimed.</aside><h2 id=\"section-1\">Use the current skills outline</h2><p>Open Microsoft's official DP-600 study guide and note its current revision date. Create a checklist from that outline rather than treating a static blog syllabus as authoritative. Product features and assessment scope can change. This independent plan does not reproduce exam questions, claim privileged exam information or guarantee a passing result.</p><h2 id=\"section-2\">Prepare a small analytics dataset</h2><p>Create a fictional sales file with five order lines, a date field, product keys and numeric amounts. Keep an independent control total. Load and prepare it in an environment you are authorized to use, documenting types, rejected values and the fact-table grain. Introduce a duplicate key in a separate test version and explain why the reconciliation fails. The goal is to understand the failure, not to make every pipeline report success.</p><h2 id=\"section-3\">Make the semantic model explainable</h2><p>Sketch the fact and dimension tables, document key uniqueness and identify the intended filter direction. Define a total and a ratio with a clear denominator. Check an unfiltered result, a single-product selection and a zero-denominator case. Explain why the grand-total ratio may differ from an average of visible row ratios. Use the official documentation to resolve uncertain behavior instead of copying an unexplained formula.</p><h2 id=\"section-4\">Test maintenance and access</h2><p>Record the data cutoff, model refresh behavior and the storage mode actually configured. Fail a source update and verify how stale data is communicated. Use an authorized viewer account to test permitted access and a restricted account to test denial. Keep screenshots or notes that show the setup and expected result without exposing real customer data or secrets.</p><h2 id=\"section-5\">Review gaps honestly</h2><p>Map each exercise back to the official outline. If you can reproduce a result only while following instructions, mark that area as needing practice. Add the relevant current Microsoft Learn resources to your plan and revisit the exercise after a break. Consult the certification page for booking and renewal information. A portfolio of understood exercises supports preparation; it does not replace Microsoft's assessment or establish professional certification by itself.</p><h2 id=\"references\">Primary references</h2><ul><li><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/certifications/resources/study-guides/dp-600\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Official DP-600 study guide</a></li><li><a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-bi/transform-model/desktop-relationships-understand\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Power BI relationships</a></li></ul>",
